      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "POLLY HOFFA (4) brings the most reliable recent profile, having won a Class 3 at this venue two starts ago before another sound third over 1200m at this track. The move back to 900m is supported by a proven track-and-distance record, and the apprentice claim strengthens a case built on consistent recent form. EGYPTIAN LASS (3) is the main danger on grade relief, with her Mackay Class 2 run better than the finishing position suggests given she was only beaten four and a half lengths at long odds. The 900m record is the query, but her prior defeat at this venue came after blundering at the start, so there is scope to rebound. IT'S A POWER (8) has placed at both runs this campaign in Mdn grade and now gets weight relief third-up, though she still has to turn consistent placings into a winning BM50 performance. LEUCAENA (5) has been plain at her latest Class B runs, but first-time blinkers and a strong placing profile at 900m give her a realistic minor-money path.",
